# Owning plan 08-01 (D-32): cases of the release-assets step, the selftest of tools/check/release-assets.sh.
# One case name per line; the step runs exactly these and fails on a name it does not know.
# Every case but outer-name-pass, version-agree-pass and changelog-section-pass must fail for its intended token;
# those three are the positive cases and must pass. The five last cases belong to plan 08-02 (D-30).
source-extra-member
source-missing-member
install-extra-member
rom-member
outer-name-pass
version-skew
version-tag-form
version-agree-pass
changelog-section-missing
changelog-section-pass
# Owning plan 08-02: the readiness script selftest (real inventory only; the toy tree has no readiness script).
readiness-selftest
# Plan 15-02 (TOOL-08, D-48, D-49, GUARDRAILS-v0.3 V6): a synthetic archive whose own list names
# lib/libivs_retro.so must still be refused as release-assets-binary-member, with no extra-member or
# missing-member finding - the binary rule does not consult the list, so no build-only host artifact can
# enter a release archive.
so-member
# Plan 18-02 (TOOL-02, D-52): a synthetic install archive carrying an extensionless bin/ivs-inspect the list does
# not name is refused as release-assets-extra-member by the EXISTING extra-member limb, and the case also requires
# that neither release-assets-binary-member nor release-assets-missing-member fired - the extension-only binary rule
# cannot see a name with no dot, so this is the phase's one release-assets case and it replaces the .ivst archive
# case rather than joining it (the .ivst refusal is already proved by the files-unlisted-binary-ivst control).
inspect-unlisted-member
